      "subtopic": "Discriminant",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "How many real solutions does ${{coef(a,'x^2')}} {{term(b,'x')}} {{signed(c)}} = 0$ have? Justify with the discriminant.",
      "answer": "{{ifelse(b*b - 4*a*c > 0, 'Two real solutions', ifelse(b*b - 4*a*c == 0, 'One repeated real solution', 'No real solutions'))}} — the discriminant is ${{b*b - 4*a*c}}$.",
